			<div class="content" id="post-content-4248606">
									

<blockquote>
<p>This piece does so much of what this site has been lacking lately. It takes a concept/anomaly/whatever and treats it as the Foundation would: cold and head-on. Nothing meta. No -J parading as an anomaly because it's created by POI's/GOI's whose whole thing is making joke anomalies. No interviews that should just be a Tale, wearing an SCP format just to be on the Mainlist.</p>
</blockquote>
<p>I'm gonna disagree with this bit here in a general sense. While yes, meta and funny articles are more accepted on the mainlist than they were ten years ago, they've mostly always been a part of the SCP format. If every article were like this (an epic Lovecraftian cosmic mystery), then this would not be an exceptional piece because it would have gotten stale after ten years of the same stuff, no matter the quality.</p>
<p>SCP is a format, and the creative things that authors do with (and sometimes despite) that format is what keeps this site interesting. Its cool to praise stuff for being different, but I can't say I agree with tearing down other valid (and successful) styles of articles to accomplish said praise.</p>

							</div>

								
